name: Mandate
description: |
  Base executable document type for guaranteed authority delegation.

  The actor bound to authorityHolderChannel controls the authority or resource
  being delegated. The actor bound to authorizedActorChannel receives the
  delegated authority. The actor bound to mandateGuarantorChannel confirms that
  the declared authority relationship is legitimate and may terminate the
  mandate.

  Authority confirmation and activation are separate lifecycle facts.
  Confirmation records that the guarantor accepted the authority declaration.
  Activation records the timestamp from which the authorized actor may use the
  delegated authority.

  By default, successful authority confirmation requests immediate activation.
  A mandate may set activateOnAuthorityConfirmation to false and define
  additional deterministic workflows that emit Mandate/Mandate Activation
  Requested when a later condition is satisfied.

  The base type defines and implements initialization, authority confirmation,
  activation, termination, lifecycle event emission, lifecycle transition
  guards, and graceful mandate-document termination. Subtypes inherit these
  lifecycle implementations unchanged. They may add specialized fields,
  validation, participants, embedded documents, and workflows that emit the
  standard activation or termination request Messages.

status:
  type: Coordination/Status
  description: |
    Current lifecycle status of the mandate.

    Initialization sets exactly one initial status:

    - Coordination/Status Pending when deterministic initialization succeeds.
    - Coordination/Status Failed when deterministic initialization fails.

    Supported transitions are:

    - Coordination/Status Pending -> Mandate/Status Authority Confirmed
    - Mandate/Status Authority Confirmed -> Mandate/Status Active
    - Coordination/Status Pending -> Mandate/Status Terminated
    - Mandate/Status Authority Confirmed -> Mandate/Status Terminated
    - Mandate/Status Active -> Mandate/Status Terminated

    Coordination/Status Failed and Mandate/Status Terminated are terminal.
    Lifecycle workflows do not replace timestamps or statuses after the
    corresponding transition succeeds.

initializationError:
  type: Text
  description: |
    First deterministic initialization error when status is
    Coordination/Status Failed.

    This field is absent when initialization succeeds. Initialization stops at
    the first material error rather than accumulating an error list.

activateOnAuthorityConfirmation:
  type: Boolean
  description: |
    Controls whether successful authority confirmation also requests mandate
    activation.

    When true, successful confirmation emits Mandate/Mandate Activation
    Requested, which is handled by the inherited activation workflow.

    When false, successful confirmation leaves the mandate in
    Mandate/Status Authority Confirmed. A specialized workflow must later emit
    Mandate/Mandate Activation Requested.

    When absent before initialization, the initialization workflow materializes
    true. The field is not a fixed inherited value, so a concrete mandate may
    explicitly set it to false.

authorityConfirmedAt:
  type: Integer
  description: |
    Microsecond timestamp of the root causal Coordination/Timeline Entry that
    successfully changed the mandate from Coordination/Status Pending to
    Mandate/Status Authority Confirmed.

    The value is derived by the inherited authority-confirmation workflow. It
    is never supplied by the operation request and is never replaced.

activatedAt:
  type: Integer
  description: |
    Microsecond timestamp from which the mandate entered Mandate/Status Active.

    The value is derived by the inherited activation workflow from the root
    causal Coordination/Timeline Entry that led to the accepted
    Mandate/Mandate Activation Requested Message. It is never supplied by
    the activation request and is never replaced.

terminatedAt:
  type: Integer
  description: |
    Microsecond timestamp from which the mandate entered Mandate/Status Terminated.

    The value is derived by the inherited termination workflow from the root
    causal Coordination/Timeline Entry that led to the accepted
    Mandate/Mandate Termination Requested Message. It is never supplied by
    the termination request and is never replaced.

validation:
  description: |
    Optional request-validation convention inherited by mandate subtypes.

    A concrete mandate type defines which request or event is matched by
    validation.request and which runtime component performs the validation.
    Mandate/Operation Mandate matches the Operation Request payload.
    Document-responder and MyOS mandate types may validate an entire request
    Message.

  request:
    description: |
      Optional static Blue pattern matched against the input defined by the
      concrete mandate type. When absent, static request-shape matching imposes
      no additional restriction.

      The same candidate input is passed to validation.function as the
      immutable BEX binding named request.

  function:
    entry: validateMandateRequest
    description: |
      Optional deterministic BEX validation program represented as a Blue node.
      The field intentionally has no repository-local nominal type: BEX program
      syntax and compilation are defined by the BEX specification and runtime.

      By convention, the host passes the candidate input being validated as the
      immutable BEX binding named request. Concrete mandate types define the
      semantic meaning of that input.

      When validation.function.entry is present, initialization verifies that
      validation.function.functions declares a local function with that name.
      The feeder or provider compiles and invokes the selected program when it
      validates a request. When absent, custom BEX validation is treated as
      passing.

contracts:
  mandateGuarantorChannel:
    type: Coordination/Timeline Channel
    schema:
      required: true
    description: |
      Required participant channel whose actor is the mandate guarantor.

      The guarantor confirms that the declared authority relationship is
      legitimate and may invoke the standard termination operation.

  authorityHolderChannel:
    type: Coordination/Timeline Channel
    schema:
      required: true
    description: |
      Required participant channel whose actor controls the authority or
      resource delegated by this mandate. The authority holder may invoke the
      standard termination operation.

  authorizedActorChannel:
    type: Coordination/Timeline Channel
    schema:
      required: true
    description: |
      Required participant channel whose actor receives the delegated
      authority. Concrete mandate subtypes define the delegated resource,
      action, target, or request semantics.

  mandateTerminationChannel:
    type: Coordination/Composite Timeline Channel
    channels:
      - mandateGuarantorChannel
      - authorityHolderChannel
    description: |
      Composite channel through which either the guarantor or authority holder
      may invoke terminateMandate. When one entry is eligible through both
      members, the composite produces one logical delivery.

  mandateLifecycleChannel:
    type: Lifecycle Event Channel
    description: |
      Processor-managed lifecycle channel used by the inherited initialization
      workflow.

  mandateActivationRequestedChannel:
    type: Triggered Event Channel
    description: |
      Internal triggered-event channel routing Mandate/Mandate Activation
      Requested Messages emitted by confirmation or specialized mandate
      workflows. External Timeline Entries do not enter this channel directly.

  mandateTerminationRequestedChannel:
    type: Triggered Event Channel
    description: |
      Internal triggered-event channel routing Mandate/Mandate Termination
      Requested Messages emitted by the standard termination operation or
      specialized mandate workflows.

  mandateLifecycleDefinition:
    type: Coordination/Compute Definition
    description: |
      Canonical reusable BEX implementation of mandate lifecycle transitions.
      It contains deterministic functions used by initializeMandate,
      confirmMandateAuthority, applyMandateActivation, and
      applyMandateTermination. Subtypes do not replace these functions.
    functions:
      isStatusPending:
        expr:
          $is:
            node:
              $document: /status
            pattern:
              type: Coordination/Status Pending

      isStatusAuthorityConfirmed:
        expr:
          $is:
            node:
              $document: /status
            pattern:
              type: Mandate/Status Authority Confirmed

      isStatusActive:
        expr:
          $is:
            node:
              $document: /status
            pattern:
              type: Mandate/Status Active

      hasDeclaredValidationEntry:
        expr:
          $or:
            - $not:
                $exists:
                  $document: /validation/function/entry
            - $and:
                - $isKind:
                    val:
                      $document: /validation/function/entry
                    kind: text
                - $hasKey:
                    object:
                      $document: /validation/function/functions
                    key:
                      $document: /validation/function/entry

      processingEventTimestamp:
        expr:
          $choose:
            cond:
              $and:
                - $isKind:
                    val:
                      $binding: processingEvent
                    kind: object
                - $isKind:
                    val:
                      $binding: processingEvent/timestamp
                    kind: integer
            then:
              $binding: processingEvent/timestamp

      sourceMessage:
        expr:
          $choose:
            cond:
              $isKind:
                val:
                  $event: /message
                kind: object
            then:
              $event: /message
            else:
              $event: /

      authorityConfirmedMessage:
        args:
          timestampUs:
            description: Root Timeline Entry timestamp.
          inResponseTo:
            description: Exact Message answered by this lifecycle Message.
        expr:
          type: Mandate/Mandate Authority Confirmed
          timestampUs:
            $var: timestampUs
          inResponseTo:
            $var: inResponseTo

      activationRequestedMessage:
        args:
          inResponseTo:
            description: Exact Message that caused the activation request.
        expr:
          type: Mandate/Mandate Activation Requested
          inResponseTo:
            $var: inResponseTo

      activatedMessage:
        args:
          timestampUs:
            description: Root Timeline Entry timestamp.
          inResponseTo:
            description: Accepted activation request.
        expr:
          type: Mandate/Mandate Activated
          timestampUs:
            $var: timestampUs
          inResponseTo:
            $var: inResponseTo

      terminationRequestedMessage:
        args:
          reason:
            description: Optional termination reason.
          inResponseTo:
            description: Exact Message that caused the termination request.
        expr:
          type: Mandate/Mandate Termination Requested
          reason:
            $var: reason
          inResponseTo:
            $var: inResponseTo

      terminatedMessage:
        args:
          timestampUs:
            description: Root Timeline Entry timestamp.
          reason:
            description: Optional termination reason.
          inResponseTo:
            description: Accepted termination request.
        expr:
          type: Mandate/Mandate Terminated
          timestampUs:
            $var: timestampUs
          reason:
            $var: reason
          inResponseTo:
            $var: inResponseTo

      initializeMandate:
        do:
          - $let:
              order:
                - validationEntryDeclared
                - initializationError
              vars:
                validationEntryDeclared:
                  $call:
                    function: hasDeclaredValidationEntry
                    args: {}
                initializationError:
                  $choose:
                    cond:
                      $not:
                        $var: validationEntryDeclared
                    then: validation.function.functions must declare the entry named by validation.function.entry.
          - $if:
              cond:
                $var: validationEntryDeclared
              then:
                - $appendChange:
                    op: replace
                    path: /status
                    val:
                      type: Coordination/Status Pending
                - $if:
                    cond:
                      $not:
                        $exists:
                          $document: /activateOnAuthorityConfirmation
                    then:
                      - $appendChange:
                          op: replace
                          path: /activateOnAuthorityConfirmation
                          val: true
              else:
                - $appendChange:
                    op: replace
                    path: /status
                    val:
                      type: Coordination/Status Failed
                - $appendChange:
                    op: replace
                    path: /initializationError
                    val:
                      $var: initializationError
          - $return:
              changeset:
                $changeset: true
              events:
                $events: true

      confirmMandateAuthority:
        do:
          - $let:
              order:
                - timestampUs
                - requestMessage
                - confirmationMessage
              vars:
                timestampUs:
                  $call:
                    function: processingEventTimestamp
                    args: {}
                requestMessage:
                  $call:
                    function: sourceMessage
                    args: {}
                confirmationMessage:
                  $call:
                    function: authorityConfirmedMessage
                    args:
                      timestampUs:
                        $var: timestampUs
                      inResponseTo:
                        $var: requestMessage
          - $if:
              cond:
                $and:
                  - $call:
                      function: isStatusPending
                      args: {}
                  - $isKind:
                      val:
                        $var: timestampUs
                      kind: integer
              then:
                - $appendChange:
                    op: replace
                    path: /status
                    val:
                      type: Mandate/Status Authority Confirmed
                - $appendChange:
                    op: replace
                    path: /authorityConfirmedAt
                    val:
                      $var: timestampUs
                - $appendEvent:
                    $var: confirmationMessage
                - $if:
                    cond:
                      $ne:
                        - $document: /activateOnAuthorityConfirmation
                        - false
                    then:
                      - $appendEvent:
                          $call:
                            function: activationRequestedMessage
                            args:
                              inResponseTo:
                                $var: confirmationMessage
          - $return:
              changeset:
                $changeset: true
              events:
                $events: true

      applyMandateActivation:
        do:
          - $let:
              order:
                - timestampUs
                - activationRequest
              vars:
                timestampUs:
                  $call:
                    function: processingEventTimestamp
                    args: {}
                activationRequest:
                  $event: /
          - $if:
              cond:
                $and:
                  - $call:
                      function: isStatusAuthorityConfirmed
                      args: {}
                  - $isKind:
                      val:
                        $var: timestampUs
                      kind: integer
              then:
                - $appendChange:
                    op: replace
                    path: /status
                    val:
                      type: Mandate/Status Active
                - $appendChange:
                    op: replace
                    path: /activatedAt
                    val:
                      $var: timestampUs
                - $appendEvent:
                    $call:
                      function: activatedMessage
                      args:
                        timestampUs:
                          $var: timestampUs
                        inResponseTo:
                          $var: activationRequest
          - $return:
              changeset:
                $changeset: true
              events:
                $events: true

      requestMandateTermination:
        do:
          - $let:
              order:
                - sourceMessage
                - reason
              vars:
                sourceMessage:
                  $call:
                    function: sourceMessage
                    args: {}
                reason:
                  $choose:
                    cond:
                      $isKind:
                        val:
                          $event: /message/request/reason
                        kind: text
                    then:
                      $event: /message/request/reason
                    else:
                      $event: /reason
          - $appendEvent:
              $call:
                function: terminationRequestedMessage
                args:
                  reason:
                    $var: reason
                  inResponseTo:
                    $var: sourceMessage
          - $return:
              changeset:
                $changeset: true
              events:
                $events: true

      applyMandateTermination:
        do:
          - $let:
              order:
                - timestampUs
                - terminationRequest
                - reason
                - terminable
              vars:
                timestampUs:
                  $call:
                    function: processingEventTimestamp
                    args: {}
                terminationRequest:
                  $event: /
                reason:
                  $event: /reason
                terminable:
                  $or:
                    - $call:
                        function: isStatusPending
                        args: {}
                    - $call:
                        function: isStatusAuthorityConfirmed
                        args: {}
                    - $call:
                        function: isStatusActive
                        args: {}
          - $if:
              cond:
                $and:
                  - $var: terminable
                  - $isKind:
                      val:
                        $var: timestampUs
                      kind: integer
              then:
                - $appendChange:
                    op: replace
                    path: /status
                    val:
                      type: Mandate/Status Terminated
                - $appendChange:
                    op: replace
                    path: /terminatedAt
                    val:
                      $var: timestampUs
                - $appendEvent:
                    $call:
                      function: terminatedMessage
                      args:
                        timestampUs:
                          $var: timestampUs
                        reason:
                          $var: reason
                        inResponseTo:
                          $var: terminationRequest
          - $return:
              changeset:
                $changeset: true
              events:
                $events: true

  initializeMandate:
    type: Coordination/Sequential Workflow
    channel: mandateLifecycleChannel
    event:
      type: Document Processing Initiated
    description: |
      Inherited initialization implementation.

      Normal Blue type resolution and bootstrap validate required role-channel
      bindings and lifecycle configuration. When validation.function.entry is
      present, this workflow verifies that validation.function.functions
      declares the selected local function.

      On success it materializes activateOnAuthorityConfirmation as true when
      absent, sets status to Coordination/Status Pending, and leaves
      lifecycle timestamps absent.

      On failure it sets status to Coordination/Status Failed, stores the
      first deterministic failure in initializationError, and leaves lifecycle
      timestamps absent.

      Concrete workflow steps and BEX implementation are defined in this base
      type.
    steps:
      - name: Initialize Mandate Lifecycle
        type: Coordination/Compute
        definition: mandateLifecycleDefinition
        entry: initializeMandate

  confirmMandateAuthority:
    type: Coordination/Sequential Workflow Operation
    channel: mandateGuarantorChannel
    description: |
      Inherited operation through which the guarantor confirms that the
      declared authority relationship is legitimate.

      On Coordination/Status Pending it changes status to
      Mandate/Status Authority Confirmed, records authorityConfirmedAt
      from the root causal Timeline Entry, emits Mandate/Mandate Authority
      Confirmed, and, when activateOnAuthorityConfirmation is not false, emits
      Mandate/Mandate Activation Requested.

      On Mandate/Status Authority Confirmed, Mandate/Status Active,
      Mandate/Status Terminated, or Coordination/Status Failed it performs no
      lifecycle mutation and does not replace authorityConfirmedAt.

      A guarantor may choose to use Operation Request.document and
      requireExactDocumentVersion to pin the reviewed mandate state. This base
      operation does not require or enforce that choice.

      Concrete workflow steps and BEX implementation are defined in this base
      type.
    steps:
      - name: Confirm Mandate Authority
        type: Coordination/Compute
        definition: mandateLifecycleDefinition
        entry: confirmMandateAuthority

  applyMandateActivation:
    type: Coordination/Sequential Workflow
    channel: mandateActivationRequestedChannel
    event:
      type: Mandate/Mandate Activation Requested
    description: |
      Sole authoritative mandate-activation implementation.

      On Mandate/Status Authority Confirmed it changes status to
      Mandate/Status Active, records activatedAt from the root causal Timeline
      Entry, and emits Mandate/Mandate Activated with
      inResponseTo referencing the accepted activation request when available.

      On Coordination/Status Pending, Mandate/Status Active,
      Mandate/Status Terminated, or Coordination/Status Failed it performs no
      lifecycle mutation and does not replace activatedAt.

      A request without a root causal Timeline Entry cannot establish an
      activation timestamp and must not activate the mandate.

      Concrete workflow steps and BEX implementation are defined in this base
      type.
    steps:
      - name: Apply Mandate Activation
        type: Coordination/Compute
        definition: mandateLifecycleDefinition
        entry: applyMandateActivation

  terminateMandate:
    type: Coordination/Sequential Workflow Operation
    channel: mandateTerminationChannel
    request:
      type: Mandate/Mandate Termination Requested
    description: |
      Standard termination operation available to the guarantor and authority
      holder.

      It does not write lifecycle state directly. It emits or forwards the
      normalized Mandate/Mandate Termination Requested Message so that
      applyMandateTermination remains the sole authoritative termination
      implementation.

      Specialized mandate types may add other operations or workflows that emit
      the same request Message.

      Concrete workflow steps are defined in this base type.
    steps:
      - name: Request Mandate Termination
        type: Coordination/Compute
        definition: mandateLifecycleDefinition
        entry: requestMandateTermination

  applyMandateTermination:
    type: Coordination/Sequential Workflow
    channel: mandateTerminationRequestedChannel
    event:
      type: Mandate/Mandate Termination Requested
    description: |
      Sole authoritative mandate-termination implementation.

      On Coordination/Status Pending, Mandate/Status Authority Confirmed, or
      Mandate/Status Active it changes status to Mandate/Status Terminated,
      records terminatedAt from the root causal Timeline Entry, and emits
      Mandate/Mandate Terminated, copies the accepted reason, sets
      inResponseTo to the accepted termination request when available, and
      requests graceful termination of the root processing scope after state
      updates and emitted Messages are applied.

      On Mandate/Status Terminated or Coordination/Status Failed it performs no
      lifecycle mutation and does not replace terminatedAt.

      A request without a root causal Timeline Entry cannot establish a
      termination timestamp and must not terminate the mandate.

      Concrete workflow steps, BEX implementation, and the
      Coordination/Terminate Processing step are defined in this base type.
    steps:
      - name: Apply Mandate Termination
        type: Coordination/Compute
        definition: mandateLifecycleDefinition
        entry: applyMandateTermination

  finalizeMandateTermination:
    type: Coordination/Sequential Workflow
    channel: mandateTerminationRequestedChannel
    event:
      type: Mandate/Mandate Terminated
    description: |
      Inherited terminal workflow. It runs only for the authoritative Mandate
      Terminated Message emitted after applyMandateTermination has committed the
      terminal state and lifecycle evidence, then requests graceful termination
      of the mandate processing scope.
    steps:
      - name: Gracefully Terminate Mandate Processing
        type: Coordination/Terminate Processing
        reason: Mandate terminated
